{"page":100,"verses":[{"verse_key":"4:135","surah":4,"ayah":135,"ar_uthmani":"۞ يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ كُونُوا۟ قَوَّٰمِينَ بِٱلْقِسْطِ شُهَدَآءَ لِلَّهِ وَلَوْ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِكُمْ أَوِ ٱلْوَٰلِدَيْنِ وَٱلْأَقْرَبِينَ ۚ إِن يَكُنْ غَنِيًّا أَوْ فَقِيرًا فَٱللَّهُ أَوْلَىٰ بِهِمَا ۖ فَلَا تَتَّبِعُوا۟ ٱلْهَوَىٰٓ أَن تَعْدِلُوا۟ ۚ وَإِن تَلْوُۥٓا۟ أَوْ تُعْرِضُوا۟ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"You who believe, uphold justice and bear witness to God, even if it is against yourselves, your parents, or your close relatives. Whether the person is rich or poor, God can best take care of both. Refrain from following your own desire, so that you can act justly- if you distort or neglect justice, God is fully aware of what you do.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"۞ يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا","en_gloss":"O you","transliteration":"yāayyuhā","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"who","transliteration":"alladhīna","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ءَامَنُوا۟","en_gloss":"believe[d]","transliteration":"āmanū","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":4,"ar":"كُونُوا۟","en_gloss":"Be","transliteration":"kūnū","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":5,"ar":"قَوَّٰمِينَ","en_gloss":"custodians","transliteration":"qawwāmīna","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":6,"ar":"بِٱلْقِسْطِ","en_gloss":"of justice","transliteration":"bil-qis'ṭi","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":7,"ar":"شُهَدَآءَ","en_gloss":"(as) witnesses","transliteration":"shuhadāa","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":8,"ar":"لِلَّهِ","en_gloss":"to Allah","transliteration":"lillahi","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":9,"ar":"وَلَوْ","en_gloss":"even if","transliteration":"walaw","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":10,"ar":"عَلَىٰٓ","en_gloss":"(it is) against","transliteration":"ʿalā","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":11,"ar":"أَنفُسِكُمْ","en_gloss":"yourselves","transliteration":"anfusikum","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":12,"ar":"أَوِ","en_gloss":"or","transliteration":"awi","verse_key":"4:135"},{"pos":13,"ar":"ٱلْوَٰلِدَيْنِ",